Z||000000||Gold-86SE||07-24-2000||11:04 AM||||<BR>A better explanation follows:<P>When I purchased my fiero the heater core had been bypassed in the front compart because of an obvious core leak.<P>After a misfortunate bump on the road one of the pipes that leads to the core was pierced and was spraying out coolant.  No problem, I will just bypass the thing in the engine compartment.<P>Now I have another pierced heater coolant line. This is the line that runs on the right rear wheel well. This is the line that runs from the thermostat housing to the waterpump. <BR>Have any of you had this problem and if so, how did you fix it?<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||07-24-2000||04:18 PM||||<BR>There is absolutely no one who has had this happen, that I just can't quite believe.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
